+# Pickup reminders
+
+For whoever changes pickup reminders or is about to propose sending them by email to save the SMS cost. The day
+before a pantry order's pickup slot, larder reminds the member by SMS. Written after volunteers proposed email
+reminders three times in one year, each time without knowing that email had been tried and dropped.
+
+## Channel
+
+Reminders go by SMS, `CHANNEL` in `larder/reminders.py`; the email branch there is unused. SMS costs the pantry about
+40 euros a month, and email would be free, so the switch keeps being proposed.
+
+It was tried. From April to June 2025 reminders went by email. The email provider reported that 34% of the reminder
+emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup is a packed bag
+whose fresh food goes in the bin by closing time. Many members share one phone across the family and never check
+email, but they see an SMS. Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. When it was proposed again in issue 52, the maintainers kept SMS.
+
+## Message
+
+One message per pantry order: "Your pantry order is ready for pickup" followed by the pickup slot.
